  "box_rule": {
    "version": 2,
    "text": "One box per ramp: the whole constructed ramp surface — sloped apron + detectable-warning pad + side flares.\nBottom edge: where the ramp meets the gutter or street. Top edge: where the slope levels into the sidewalk.\nExclude road/gutter pavement, level sidewalk, and neighboring ramps.\nA corner apron that point review counted as two ramps gets two boxes, one per direction of travel — overlap is fine.\nOccluded is not absent: box the inferred full extent behind cars/pedestrians; truly undeterminable -> \"Can't determine extent\".\nTight beats symmetric: every edge should touch the ramp's boundary at native zoom.\nThe box is a measuring instrument, not the crop: road and surrounding context are what a crop rule adds AROUND your box and gets scored on — never include them.\nOblique ramps (running toward the horizon): keep the box axis-aligned and touch the ramp's extremities — empty corners are correct, don't rotate-fit by eye."
  },
